    const brk = ['weak', 'unsupported', 'contradicted'].map((s) => [kept.filter((c) => c.support === s).length, s]).filter(([n]) => n).map(([n, s]) => `${n} ${s}`).join(' · ');
    const pl = d.plain || { summary: String(it.body || '').trim(), records: null };
    // One summary card: the title and its line, readiness (small, with what the unsupported claims are), the paper's summary under a quiet divider, then what holds it back.
    // The top card (the mockup approved on 19 Nov): the title, its line, then Manuscript and Delivers on the left; readiness in its own block on the right (below the title on a phone).
    // The manuscript shows its file name and opens the vault viewer (the full path in its tooltip); one this viewer cannot read shows no path at all.
    const ms = f.manuscript ? (d.sources || []).find((s) => s.text === f.manuscript) : null;
    const msFile = !f.manuscript ? '' : ms?.where === 'vault' && ms.path ? `<a class="bp-vf" href="${esc(vlHref(ms.path))}" data-vf="${esc(ms.path)}" title="${esc(ms.path)}">${esc(ms.path.split('/').pop())}</a>`
      : ms?.where === 'outside' ? `<span class="id" title="${esc(f.manuscript)}">${esc(String(f.manuscript).split(/[\\/]/).pop() || f.manuscript)}</span>` : '<span class="meta bp-na">Not available to you</span>';
    // A milestone's short name (up to 24 characters) is what Delivers shows; without one, its title cut off with an ellipsis. The tooltip holds the full title.
    const dlName = (l) => { const t = String(l.title || l.key); return l.short ? String(l.short) : t.length > 24 ? `${t.slice(0, 23).trimEnd()}…` : t; };
    const dlLinks = delivered.map((l) => `<button type="button" class="bp-inl" data-bp="${esc(bpItemArg(pid, l.key))}" title="${esc(l.title || l.key)}">${esc(dlName(l))}</button>`).join(' · ');
    const auth = (f.authors || []).map(named).join(', ');
    const hl = (k, v) => (v ? `<span class="bp-hk">${k}</span><span class="bp-hv">${v}</span>` : '');
    const lines = hl('Manuscript', msFile) + hl('Delivers', dlLinks) + hl('Authors', esc(auth));
    main = `<section class="sec bp-sec bp-pcard" aria-label="Paper summary"><div class="bp-top"><div class="bp-ph">${bpPh(it, d.plain)}<p class="meta">${meta}</p>${xr}${lines ? `<div class="bp-hl">${lines}</div>` : ''}</div>`
      + `<div class="bp-rd">${bpReady(pp)}${pp.total ? `<b>${pp.supported} of ${pp.total}</b><span class="of">claims supported</span>` : '<span class="of">No claims yet</span>'}`
      + (kept.length ? `<div class="bp-strip" role="img" aria-label="${esc(stripLabel)}">${[...kept].sort((a, b) => worst(b) - worst(a)).map((c) => `<i class="${tone(c)}"></i>`).join('')}</div>` : '<p class="meta">Confirmed results offer Add as claim.</p>')
      + (brk ? `<p class="meta bp-brk">${esc(brk)}</p>` : '') + '</div></div>'
      + (pl.summary ? `<div class="bp-psum">${overline('Summary')}${prose(pl.summary, 'bp-sum')}</div>` : '')
      + (held.length ? `<div class="bp-held">${overline('Holding it back', held.length)}${held.slice(0, 5).map(claimRow).join('')}${held.length > 5 ? `<button type="button" class="bp-more" data-bp-outline>and ${held.length - 5} more in Claims by part</button>` : ''}</div>` : '')
      + (d.standing ? bpStand(d) : '')
      + '</section>'
      + (pp.claims.length ? `<section class="sec bp-sec" id="bpOutline" tabindex="-1"><h4>Claims by part · ${pp.claims.length}</h4>${BP_PARTS.map(([k, l]) => { const L = pp.claims.filter((c) => (c.part || null) === k); return L.length ? overline(l, L.length) + L.map(claimRow).join('') : ''; }).join('')}</section>` : '')
      + (d.sources?.length ? card(`Sources · ${d.sources.length}`, bpSources(d.sources, false)) : '');
    // Records go last: under the left column on desktop, after the side cards on a phone.
    if (pl.records) tail = `<section class="sec bp-sec">${bpRec(pl.records)}</section>`;
    after.push(() => { const b = $('[data-bp-outline]'); if (b) b.onclick = () => { const o = $('#bpOutline'); o.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' }); o.focus({ preventScroll: true }); }; });
